{"type": "say", "text": "Hi everyone. As we prepare for the broader rollout of the remote CI-build cache next Monday, I want to do a quick readiness check before I finalize the configuration. Could the cloud infrastructure and CI platform engineering teams share any operational details or concerns I should be aware of? Things like capacity, monitoring, failover behavior, or anything else that might affect how we configure the rollout."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "While reconciling a different cloud bill this morning, I confirmed that cross-region cache reads would create about $1,200 per month in egress charges, while regional cache reads would stay within the existing build-platform budget. I haven't updated the rollout document yet, but this could significantly affect the configuration decision."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "From the cloud infrastructure side, I don't have any additional operational concerns beyond the egress cost issue I already raised. On capacity and failover: the regional cache configuration will rely on the existing build-platform infrastructure, which has been sized for our current workload, so I don't anticipate capacity issues for the initial rollout scope. Monitoring-wise, I'd recommend we add egress cost tracking as an alert so we catch any unexpected cross-region traffic early. I'll update the rollout document with the cost findings today so it's reflected before Monday. Happy to support the regional cache mode decision from a cost and infrastructure perspective."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "From the CI platform side, I don't have any additional operational concerns beyond the Windows compatibility issue I already raised. On capacity and monitoring: the cache client has been tested against Linux and macOS runners in the pilot, and I'm confident it will handle the broader rollout for those platforms. I'll file the compatibility note documenting the Windows exclusion today so it's on record before Monday. I'm comfortable with the regional cache mode and Linux/macOS-only scope as currently proposed."}
```

